<title>UK: UK Dec net consumer credit up s/a 1.022 bln stg.</title>
<headline>UK Dec net consumer credit up s/a 1.022 bln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England released the following seasonally-adjusted consumer credit data.</p>
<p>-NET LENDING (previously released data in brackets, in MLN stg)</p>
<p>					    Dec	 Nov	     Dec 95</p>
<p> Total net lending		    2,625     2,841 (2,825)  2,115</p>
<p> -- Consumer credit		   1,022     1,050 (1,105)    836</p>
<p> -- On dwellings			1,603     1,791 (1,720)  1,279</p>
<p>BREAKDOWN OF NET CONSUMER LENDING BY SOURCE</p>
<p> -- Banks				 459	 807  (868)	 465</p>
<p> -- Building Soc			 33	  23  (23)	   32</p>
<p> -- Other specialist lenders	525	 223  (213)	 369</p>
<p> -- Retailers			     8	  -1  (2)	   -26</p>
<p> -- Insurance co			 -3	  -2  (-1)	   -4</p>
<p> -- Credit card			 184	 361  (339)	 286</p>
<p>CONSUMER CREDIT (seasonally adjusted in pct)</p>
<p>					    DECEMBER	  NOVEMBER</p>
<p> Consumer credit mth/mth		1.4		1.5  (1.5)</p>
<p>		     3mth annualised   17.6	     18.2 (18.4)</p>
<p>		     6mth annualised   18.8	     17.8 (18.0)</p>
<p>		     year-on-year	16.6	     16.5 (16.6)</p>
<p> Total Personal borrowing mth/mth   0.5		0.6  (0.6)</p>
<p>		     3mth annualised    7.2		7.2  (7.1)</p>
<p>		     6mth annualised    7.0		6.9  (6.8)</p>
<p>		     year-on-year	 6.4		6.4  (6.3)</p>
<p> Secured on Dwellings mth/mth	 0.4		0.4  (0.4)</p>
<p>		     3mth annualised    5.4		5.4  (5.2)</p>
<p>		     6mth annualised    5.1		5.1  (5.0)</p>
<p>		     year-on-year	 4.8		4.7  (4.7)</p>
<p>Note - Consensus forecast was for a 958 million stg rise in net credit.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
